    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] For over a decade the Hartman Theatre Company served as one of the nation’s leading regional theatres and was the recipient of a special Drama Desk Award for Producing Unprecedented Work, such as the pre-Broadway production of The Runner Stumbles in the theatre’s premiere season.\n[2] In 2001, Dame Helen Mirren and Dame Judi Dench joined MTG’s Board of Advisors.\n[3] On television she starred opposite John Lithgow as Clementine Churchill in \"The Crown\" (2016), Natalie Chandler in the ITV drama series \"\" (2009–14), and as Lady Prudence Shackleton in four episodes of \"Downton Abbey\" (2013–15).\n[4] In 2012, German theatre educator and actress Claudia Jessat joined the company and the two of them managed the company together until Gareth's passing in early 2016, after which Claudia assumed the role of the owner."
